-- Passage rg5-character-setting-plot-p08
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('19e13ce0-cd81-5358-958e-a69a435b310d', 'rg5-character-setting-plot-p08', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g5-character-setting-plot'), null,
        '3-5', $q$Saturday at the Clay Studio$q$, $q$Every Saturday, Nia Adeyemi and Ravi Menon took a pottery class at the Maple Street Arts Center. The studio smelled like wet earth, and gray dust covered every shelf.

Nia was careful and serious. She wanted each bowl to be perfectly round. If a rim tilted even a little, she squashed the clay into a ball and started over. In six weeks, she had finished only one bowl.

Ravi was cheerful and curious. His bowls leaned, bulged and wobbled, but he kept every one. He gave them names like Leaning Larry and Mr. Lumpy. By the sixth week, his shelf was crowded with odd little pots.

One Saturday, their teacher, Mr. Fontaine, announced a show for families. Each student would display five pieces. Ravi picked his five favorites in a minute. Nia looked at her single bowl and felt her stomach drop.

"I don't have enough," she whispered.

Ravi slid one of her squashed clay balls toward her. "Then make some fast ones," he said. "Just for fun."

So Nia did. She let a rim tilt. She left a thumbprint on a cup. To her surprise, she liked them. Each one looked like it had a story.

At the show, Nia's five pieces sat beside Ravi's. Her grandmother picked up the tilted cup and smiled. "This one looks like you made it with your hands," she said. "Not with a machine."$q$, 'draft')
